e brother of Michah was Isshiah: of the sons of Isshiah; Zechariah.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙCThe sons of Merari were Mahli and Mushi: the sons of Jaaziah; Beno.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙFThe sons of Merari by Jaaziah; Beno, and Shoham, and Zaccur, and Ibri.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ'Of Mahli came Eleazar, who had no sons.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ/Concerning Kish: the son of Kish was Jerahmeel.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ{The sons also of Mushi; Mahli, and Eder, and Jerimoth. These were the sons of the Levites after the house of their fathers.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses‘„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙüThese likewise cast lots over against their brethren the sons of Aaron in the presence of David the king, and Zadok, and Ahimelech, and the chief of the fathers of the priests and Levites, even the principal fathers over against their younger brethren.¦layout ªlast_verse